  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Campusano walked it off in the eleventh after trailing through seven innings.",
    "what_this_means": "The Padres needed an eighth-inning tying run to stay alive, then pushed two across in the eleventh to end it. That's the shape of a game that had no margin for error and no patience for early leads. Bogaerts opened the scoring with a solo home run, but it wasn't enough ballast for a lineup that went quiet in the fourth and ninth with runners in position. The bullpen did the heavy lifting. Five relievers covering seven innings without allowing a run, with Adrian Morejon striking out four in the final two frames. But a win built on a late rally carries its own weight. One more inning of Milwaukee pressure, one more miss in the eighth, and this stays a loss. Close games are what surge looks like from the inside, but they're also what collapses feel like when the margin disappears.",
